TY  - JOUR
AU  - Shuyu Shen
AU  - Chen Yan
AU  - Yilei Qian
TI  - Syndication with government and follow-on investment decision of private venture capital
JO  - Applied Economics Letters
PY  - 2026
AB  - Using a round-by-round dataset of China’s venture capital market between 2006 and 2024, we find that syndicating with Government Venture Capital (GVC) is significantly associated with a reduced probability of follow-on investment by incumbent Private Venture Capital (PVC). This negative association is inconsistent with generalized crowding-out by competition for high-quality assets, but rather correlates with concerns about risk and hold-up costs. This study advances understanding of GVC beyond the initial formation of syndicates to the continuity of private capital investment, while leaving scope for further improvements in causal identification and data coverage.
DO  - 10.1080/13504851.2026.2741409
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1080/13504851.2026.2741409
N1  - [관련도 88] Using a round-by-round dataset of China’s venture capital market between 2006 and 2024, we find that syndicating with Government Venture Capital (GVC) is significantly associated with a reduced probability of follow-on investment by incumbent Private Venture Capital (PVC).
